[i]Version 3.4.0[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v3.4.0 🛠️ARCHITECTURE & OPTIMIZATION UPDATE!🛠️[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ CORE ARCHITECTURE PATCH[/b]
[i]This update implements Progressive Materialization to eliminate massive lag spikes![/i]

[b]🛠️ ARCHITECTURE & OPTIMIZATION[/b]
[list]
[*]⚡ [b]Progressive Materialization (Lag Fix):[/b] Completely overhauled the [i]CosmicVaultTerritory[/i] API. When AI factions expand or background sieges are won, the game no longer forcefully loads the sector into memory to generate stations (which caused brutal server stutters).
[*]⚡ [b]Lazy Loading API:[/b] Stations and sector flips are now queued mathematically. When a player jumps into the affected sector, the game seamlessly intercepts the loading screen and instantly materializes the stations. Zero stutter!
[/list]

[i]Version 3.3.3[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v3.3.3 🐛CRITICAL BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix targets a critical server hanging issue during combat and a Fleet Clash scaling bug![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Fleet Clash AI Scaling Bug:[/b] Fixed a syntax error during dynamic AI Fleet battles where the backend script was checking for [code]Entity.isPlayer[/code] (an invalid property) instead of [code]entity.playerOwned[/code], which caused the Fleet Clash event to fail scaling its defender strength and throw errors.
[*]🐛 [b]Combat Server Hang / Freeze:[/b] Fixed a massive server lag spike and 30-second sector freezing caused by an invalid [code]Uuid[/code] string serialization error inside [i]cosmicdot.lua[/i]. When sectors unloaded and reloaded, the Damage Over Time effect would corrupt its source ID, breaking the engine's durability calculation and hanging the server thread.
[/list]

[i]Version 3.3.2[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v3.3.2 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
